{"id":"tb-cl10","capability":"translate_body","author":"地理编辑（气候与观测数据 beat）","what":"全文翻译人工稿：cl10（IMBIE 那条：Faster-flowing glaciers fuel decades of polar ice loss）。translate_body 的请求体只有 segments，匹配域里没有标题与网址，故键只能取正文连续片段。","match":{"textIncludes":["ice-sheet change","11 trillion"]},"reply":{"segmentMap":[{"includes":"The longest satellite data record of ice-sheet change ever assembled","zh":"这是迄今汇编的最长一段卫星冰盖变化数据记录，显示格陵兰（Greenland）与南极（Antarctica）自 1970 年代以来共失去 11 trillion 吨冰，使全球海平面上升超过 3 厘米"},{"includes":"Ice Sheet Mass Balance Intercomparison Exercise (IMBIE)","zh":"最新结果发表于《Nature》旗下期刊 Scientific Data，来自冰盖质量收支互比试验（IMBIE，Ice Sheet Mass Balance Intercomparison Exercise），是一项汇集全球多国机构极地科学家的大型国际合作"},{"includes":"data from 27 satellite missions","zh":"研究依托 27 个卫星任务的数据，其中包括 ESA 的 CryoSat"},{"includes":"the glaciers that drain these vast ice sheets are also flowing faster","zh":"新结果同时表明，事情并不只是冰盖表面融化，排送这些巨大冰盖的冰川也在流动得更快，把大量冰直接注入海洋"}]}}
